{
  "id": "sensory-bias",
  "term": "sensory bias",
  "definition": "Sensory bias is a tendency in an animal’s sensory or cognitive processing that makes some kinds of stimuli stand out more than others, leading to stronger responses to those more relevant cues. This bias can help the animal judge which signals are most important and choose an appropriate behaviour.",
